<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head">
      <h2>Nobody wants to hand an AI the keys to prod. Good.</h2>
      <p>That instinct is correct — and it’s exactly the problem Turf is built around.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="beats">
      <div class="beat">
        <span class="k">01 · The fear is rational</span>
        <h3>Unconstrained agents are click-ops at machine speed</h3>
        <p>An agent holding raw cloud credentials mutates infrastructure with <b>no diff, no review,
        and no state</b> — the same failure mode as console click-ops, only faster.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="beat">
        <span class="k">02 · The reframe</span>
        <h3>Turf doesn’t put AI in control — it puts AI under control</h3>
        <p>The governing instrument is the <b>industry-standard Terraform plan</b>. Turf constrains
        the agent to work in terms of plans and their effects. Nothing runs off-plan.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="beat">
        <span class="k">03 · What you get</span>
        <h3>Visibility · Governance · Flexibility</h3>
        <p>Every proposed change is <b>visible before it happens</b>, gated on <b>your approval</b>,
        and applied <b>one effect at a time</b> — with room to pause, back up, or re-plan.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
